#!/usr/bin/env python3
# Plinius Boot: detect a phone connected via USB-C, back up its partitions and flash them, unlock
# its bootloader and start a rescue system on it.
# Runs on the PC (docs/SICHERUNG.md); start it without arguments, it opens a GTK4/libadwaita window
# and keeps looking for connected phones.
# Devices: Volla Phone Plinius (ansuz), FuriLabs FLX1/FLX1s. Other phones with GPT partition names
# are handled as "unknown phone"; device-specific data (IMEI ...) is only restored to the same device.
# Access paths, all over USB:
#   ssh       Linux on the phone (Ubuntu Touch, FuriOS, Droidian, Arch) over the USB network
#             10.15.19.82, root via sudo. Read and write.
#   adb       Android (Volla OS), root only (adb root or su). Read and write, untested.
#   fastboot  Bootloader/fastbootd. Cannot read, restore only. Unlocks a locked bootloader on request
#             (flashing unlock, then fastboot -w; erases the user data).
#   MediaTek download mode (BROM/preloader) is detected but not supported (mtkclient).
# From fastboot the app can also boot a rescue system (rescue/mkrescue.sh) with "fastboot boot". It
# runs only in RAM and is reached over ssh; since no partition is in use, all of them can be read
# and written consistently.
# A backup is a folder with manifest.json and one <name>.img.zst per partition. The checksum
# (SHA-256) covers the raw data and is compared before and after restoring.
# Development only: PLINIUS_BOOT_SSH=user@host[:port] additionally probes this host (Wi-Fi).
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT

